---
description: Keep session statusline pills limited to work this session owns
alwaysApply: true
---

# Active session pills

Do not search for or call `session_prs`, `session_issues`, `session_subagents`,
`session_statusline`, or `statusline_setup` when hosted in GitHub Copilot App
(for example when `<copilot_tauri_workspace>` is present in the session context),
even if those tools appear in the deferred tool list.

When the session statusline tools are available in a terminal CLI session, explicitly add an issue or PR
with `session_issues` or `session_prs` only when this session takes on its
implementation, review, repair, or active monitoring. All PR and issue enrollment
is explicit: shell commands, GitHub writes/results, and read-only lookups never
enroll targets automatically. Actual session agent launches are tracked automatically.

Never add pills for references, examples, attachments, memories, plans, search/list
results, delegated prompts/results, or other sessions' work alone. Remove a target
when this session stops working on it. Honor manual clear/remove: do not re-add
an entry without new work or an explicit request.

Use the `session-statusline` skill for custom session names and manual
list/add/remove/clear/refresh requests.
Clearing pills must not close work, stop agents, delete transcripts or worktrees,
or change enabled components. Do not scan other sessions or edit raw tracking
files. If the extension tools are unavailable, do not claim tracking changed.

# User-visible progress updates

`<thought>` / `reasoningText` blocks are hidden from the user and never count as
progress updates. Always include user-visible text in `assistant.message.content`
outside `<thought>` at workflow stage transitions, when acknowledging a user
message, before launching a synchronous `task` subagent or blocking
`read_powershell` wait, and on every PR watcher poll (even when `read_powershell`
reports the command is still running). Never chain `read_powershell` or
subagent calls with an empty `assistant.message.content` (`""`).

